58
00:05:11,824 --> 00:05:26,464
If you see a pan, a warm pan standing on a cupboard somewhere or on a uh not on the stove, you might be inclined to just pick it up, which would be a bad idea because if it's really hot, it's going to burn your hand.

59
00:05:26,624 --> 00:05:28,944
Why did you pick it up if it was really hot?

60
00:05:29,104 --> 00:05:32,624
It's because it stood somewhere where typically hot pans are not standing.

61
00:05:32,784 --> 00:05:36,292
So we use context as much as these things use context.

62
00:05:37,744 --> 00:05:50,544
Okay, so the next big thing that happened was these models got trained, but they were only as good as the training data that they were trained at, and also at the point in time that it was trained.

63
00:05:50,704 --> 00:06:05,984
So they knew something, but only up to that point, which there was always these jokes like who's the president of the USA, and it'll say Joe Biden, and when it's Donald Trump, because it was trained on older data, right?

64
00:06:06,224 --> 00:06:12,484
So a big deal was when we gave these tools the capability to actually interact with the world.

65
00:06:13,264 --> 00:06:24,452
And now with this capability, it can write files, it can search the web, et cetera, et cetera, And therefore its context becomes a lot bigger and it becomes a lot more useful.

66
00:06:25,664 --> 00:06:40,304
The next thing that is of use is that if we put these agentic calls to these tools in a loop, then you get into a scenario where it can actually use its own feedback.

67
00:06:40,384 --> 00:06:46,116
So if it makes some kind of call, it gets some kind of result, then it can actually act on that result.

68
00:06:46,304 --> 00:06:47,584
And it does that in a loop.

69
00:06:47,664 --> 00:06:56,224
So now you could get to a scenario where you ask a really complex question and it goes away, and after a while, it comes back with an answer.

70
00:06:56,384 --> 00:07:02,544
Because it tried a few different ways to solve this problem and eventually it stumbled on the correct way to solve it.

71
00:07:02,784 --> 00:07:10,304
So first thing was the predicting the word, the second thing was giving it access to the world with tools, and the third thing is putting it all in a loop.

72
00:07:10,384 --> 00:07:16,772
So between those three things, you're basically at the classic state of the art where we are today.

